{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213907,"nonce":"O0vN0plUTT0dVRv6beQgH/W+5Ls=","title":"Benchmarks and publishing shaped like Ash's","message":"- bench/benchmarks.toml manifest: [[mode]] rows (interpreter, tiered, aot) and [[bench]] rows each carrying an accepted checksum set with labels; judge every iteration; report INVALID separately from FAIL/TIMEOUT and exclude it from speedups.\n- Mirror Ash's corpus so numbers line up: fib(40) single call printing 102334155 plus a fib_calls variant if pure-call CSE ever collapses it; binary_trees n=16 with the XOR-fold checksum; deltablue 40 x (chainTest(100)+projectionTest(100)) printing 14065400; nbody 10M steps printing int(energy*1e6) = -169077; the four call kernels (inlined/free/method/closure) at 100M iterations of sum = sum*31 + (i%8) with an explicit 32-bit wrap so the -1737346944 checksum reproduces, receiver from a runtime-opaque source; mandelbrot 875x500x1000 with a checksum band. Keep the existing depth-14 rows for continuity.\n- Harness: fresh process per run, warmups documented as OS warmups, median headline with min/max/sd, bimodal split at the widest gap above 10%, RSS and GC counters from a separate instrumented run, strip profiling env vars, record load average and CPU model.\n- Regression gate: median grows by both \u003e 10% and \u003e 5 ms, or status worsens.\n- CI: build once and ship binaries as an artifact, one runner per benchmark with fail-fast off, comparison lanes (wren_cli, AOT) after the engine under test, daily schedule not per push, in-sweep A/B against the previous sweep's commit, always-run aggregate to a schema-versioned JSON, page normalises to the reference row as 1.00x.\n\n- Rolling nightly GitHub release rebuilt on a schedule and marked latest; versioned releases on v* tags; install.sh / install.ps1 try latest then nightly, write an env file, append to the shell rc. Ship the checksums (Ash generates but does not upload them) and ship the static runtime archive so `wlift build` of a plugin-free program works from an installed release (Ash's tarball omits it and that path fails).\n- `wlift build` decides static vs shared runtime from whether the program loads plugins; stamp the shared runtime's install_name/soname at its own build so staging is a copy; embed the shared runtime bytes in the compiler so --build works on a machine that never built the workspace.\n- AOT-vs-tiered byte-for-byte smoke on ubuntu, ubuntu-arm, macos, windows with per-invocation timeouts and file-backed capture.\n- Site deployed from CI artifacts with upload-pages-artifact, no gh-pages branch; refuse to publish an empty table.","files":null}]}